e4f2cfa5ebff863a4d5d13c040cb0c41be6a40f9:corpus/lessons/round-46.md:19:| M46-3 | `freeze-moved-four-times` — the freeze commit `3182047` did not contain the bytes that could be scored: the guard returned an int where the caller unpacked a tuple, `run_battery` referenced a renamed regex and could only fail, and the v1 registry profile applied the v2 strict checks to historical rows. Three further commits (`50862e4a`, `65678df0`, `04252247`) were needed before a counter produced a verdict, so the freeze is a series and the claims plan's "the commit that first contains this file and tools/round-46/" is false for the declared freeze. | `plans/round-46-claims.md` (freeze definition) against the four commits; each defect has its own receipt: the do-nothing control exiting 2 `battery: cannot build a battery`, `NameError: name 'REF' is not defined`, and `thin verdict-map cells: 6` in `l1/scores/` | `none` in the instrument — the selftest ran with `with_battery=False`, so `run_battery` was never executed by any case, and no gate compared the freeze commit with the bytes it was supposed to freeze | the selftest now carries a `green-with-battery` case (16 cases), and the criterion is `QUALITY.md` row 77: an instrument is frozen only when the path its claim scores has been EXECUTED once, not merely imported |
